Z||000003||fastonpumpgas||10-16-1999||07:26 AM||||I argee I would be pretty pissed, considering if you order something from Summit it is overnight.  I ended up porting my exhaust manifolds, i mean , I dont see that much more of a gain unless you are going all out.  Unless you just wantt the look. I heard the fiero store takes a long time too||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave85||10-16-1999||10:50 AM||||Everything I've ordered from Fiero Store comes FED_EX. Don't know about headers though. <BR>As far as Chris West goes, he may be a great guy BUT, if people are having problems getting stuff then we should be made aware of that. You wouldn't think twice about saying something if it was someone you didn't know.<BR>This Fourm is by far the best tool that any Fiero owner can have.  If you have a good/bad experience then I'd like to know about it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Boxdin||10-16-1999||01:56 PM||||The previous note convinced me, I'vee got to relate my experience with FOCOA. I ordered 1500 bucks worth of stuff, including headers. My card was charged immediately. FOUR months later, after I notify them I'm stopping the credit card transaction, they ship the wrong goods. I ship back, except for 165.00 worth I really needed. They now have the parts, and my money !! I'm thankful my credit card co is fighting for me, although slowly. I looked at the headers for the short time I had them, and they looked beautiful. But they had huge ports, and were not "anti-reversionary" .  I was taught you have to have some velocity in order to scvange the port completely, and that came with the right size tube. <BR>( documentation provided upon request )||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pretender||10-18-1999||02:24 AM||||in the other forums that my friends surf *imports* they have a list of from who to buy from and who not. This is a great idea! I had a bad experiance with the used parts guy that the fiero store guy referred me to for good used parts. I called him up and ordered an oil pan which was sent out quickly(same day i think) but when i had gotten it the MORON SPRAY PAINTED THE WHOLE THING! INSIDE AND OUT! I don't remember his name nor have his phone number but i think it was on a farm or something like that. what a really dumb moron, i had to send it out to have it sand blasted. MORON!||||reg||1
Z||000007||GWMORGAN||10-18-1999||02:33 AM||||Pretender,<BR>  The name of the guy is Bob and the place is Kick Hill Farm.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||10-18-1999||01:30 PM||||GW, unless the pans are coated with something, they will rust in storage. Kick Hill Farm actually inventories individual parts. Unless you want a pan covered in rust.<P>There is nothing wrong with painting both sides of the pan. If you don't like it painted inside or don't trust the paint not to flake off then remove it. It's not hard.<P>I'd rather spend a few minutes taking off some paint, than sanding off rust for an hour only to find a pit that's gone thru.||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||10-18-1999||08:11 PM||||I too was getting annoyed at Chris West for being slow getting an order out. I ordered a battery relocating box from him over 2 1/2 months ago and just got it today. At one point he said I never sent payment, but my Credit Union had a copy of the cleared check. Next, he stated in an email on 9-8-99 that he would ship it right out, but I never heard from him again. He never answered my last three emails. Then, just as I was getting really mad, the package arrives out of nowhere today. You'd think he could have sent me an occassional message to update me on the delays and to assure me that I was not forgotten.||||reg||1
