Z||000013||Pretender||10-19-1999||03:18 AM||||the way i see it is that if your oil pan is painted on the inside your just asking for trouble. Sooner or later that paint is going to chip and travel through your engine causing lots of money that you could probably use fixing other things on your car besides $1000s of labour charges. The paint in my pan was actually chipping and was probably K-mart 99 cent special. ||||reg||10
Z||000014||88 Fiero||10-20-1999||10:44 AM||||All I can say is that when you buy this aftermarket stuffs be sure your money is worth spending. Like this headers thing... Chris'es headers are FOCOA knock offs... I know this because I know both parties out here in California. The difference between this 2 headers is that Chris took a short-cut on his headers. FOCOA is still being build by the same guy who does headers for the Buick Grand Nationals.. Price difference wise...FOCOA is $550.00 and Chris'es is $444.00. For a mere difference of $106.00. I would save and spend that extra money for a set of headers that has been proven and dynoed....FOCOA... I know it sucks when you order and it takes awhile. Thank God I live close to them...But it's worth it... I am buying my headers thru FOCOA on December....Just a comment for everyone....||||reg||1
Z||000015||terryk||10-20-1999||09:11 PM||||The Chevy Power Book gives information on "real" headers for the 660 engine. I am disappointed on the limited room to put full length headers in a Fiero engine bay.<P>At the same time, $550 (or $444 for that matter) doesn't give enough HP/$. A good cam, 1.6L:1 rockers and the like are a better deal. <P>Now we just need to drill a hole in the shock tower to get the cam out!||||reg||1
Z||000016||88 Fiero||10-20-1999||10:02 PM||||terryk...when I bought my '88 the guy who sold me told me that he put a performance cam in it.. I ask him if he pulled the engine out... He said no... He cut the firewall and pull the cam on the side and put the new one in... He even showed me where he pulled it...very interesting....||||reg||1
